00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
 
does age matter  when i was in my first business it was a  biotech software company  i was 19 years old i had no idea what i  was doing  and i was afraid to sell  i was afraid that people wouldn't take  me seriously here i was i was i was 19.  i was selling the people who had phds  who were two or three times my age who  were experts in their field  i had no science background no computer  background  and i felt like i was completely  mismatched  it was me my two business partners  working out of an apartment  grinding it out and i was afraid that  if any of my clients actually saw what  what our company infrastructure was  they would be shocked and would not want  to talk to me they wouldn't want to buy  from us i had a great looking website  we looked professional from the web but  what we were actually doing i was i was  embarrassed by it  i didn't want people to find out i  didn't feel comfortable talking to  people  on the phone meeting people i just  wasn't confident enough in it  i thought i was too young  and i remember the moment where that  changed where i realized that it's not  about how old you are  it's just about your confidence and if  you can actually provide something of  value  the moment for me came when i was  working on a deal to distribute  my software in the uk a company had come  to us  and they wanted to represent they wanted  to represent us  in the uk i didn't really care so much  about the uk most my business was  to us and canada and uk was a great you  know little  piece but i didn't really care so much  they wanted exclusive rights  so i told them you know what if you give  me  13 and a half thousand dollars up front  i'll give you exclusive rights to the uk  and you get your commissions you get all  leads that come from the uk and i  thought  whatever like they're going to take that  and i thought  you know give it away who cares i'm  working on trying to build this business  in u.s and canada and they wrote back  and they said let's do it and i was  shocked  that was big money for me maybe that's  not a lot to you guys but when i was  starting up  i was like 300 a month this was 13  and a half thousand dollars this was  this was like winning the lottery for me  this was huge  this man i could i could eat you know  this man i could hang out with my  friends a little bit i'm not talking  luxury lifestyle just  any kind of lifestyle this deal got me  there  and i realized that they didn't care how  old i was  what they cared about was that i had  something of value for them  i had something that could help and they  wanted a part of it  and after that deal my mindset changed  and i realized that  it doesn't matter that my customers are  two or three times my age and they have  much better education than i do  and that they know their field way  better than i do  it doesn't matter because the tool that  i was selling could help them  and at the end of the day that's all  they cared about too nobody asked me hey  do you have a phd like i do  hey do you understand genetics like i do  no they didn't care they only cared that  i could help them with the problem and i  could do that  so it doesn't matter how old you are  people don't care what they care about  is can you help them  if you can help me then i want to listen  to you and i don't care  what your background is i don't care  what country you're from  i don't care if you have a disability or  not i don't care if english is your  second language i don't care about any  of that stuff that's all in your head  none of that stuff matters it doesn't  matter all people care about is can you  help them  if you can then they'll want to work  with you  and as soon as you get over that  limiting belief in your head  you'll start having bigger success  this comes out of a question from one of  my newsletter readers rashid who wrote  in saying  do years determine the level of success  and accumulating wealth because most of  the entrepreneurs the great  entrepreneurs i know  are in their late 50s  let's break that up if you're just  talking about accumulating wealth  the typical way people do that is  through investing right  and the more time you have the more your  money can work for you and it's easier  to make money  but if you're talking about  entrepreneurship  you don't have to be in your late 50s to  have success as an entrepreneur most of  the great  companies that are coming out now are  from young people they're people in  their 20s  who have revolutionary ideas and new  ways of seeing things  and they put that to work you have to  just have the confidence  that's what i was lacking i didn't have  confidence  i was so worried and hung up on my age  and how people would perceive me that i  didn't even try  i avoided talking to customers talking  to partners talking to media as much as  possible  because i was scared and i didn't have  any self-confidence  in what we were doing and i just wanted  the product to speak for itself so it's  so important  if you're in that place now if you think  you're too young  or too old or too whatever  it's in your head it doesn't matter  people don't care about it  all they care about again is can you  help them and if you know you can  then you walk into every meeting with  confidence because you're not selling  them now  you don't have to convince them about  anything you know that you can help them  that confidence comes through that  passion comes through  that commitment comes through and  they're going to want to do business  with you  believe you guys like this video please  give it a thumbs up below it always  makes me want to do more and please  leave a comment underneath man you  those comments mean the world to me i  wake up every day with them i love  seeing them so please leave a comment  let me know what you think  leaving comments spur people like me on  so get it going below you have a  question leave it below i'll make a  video response thank you so much and  i'll see you soon

